// ADR 0025 S1 — THE ABUSE DIRECTION OF THE SPELLABILITY LAYER.
//
// `CtrLeafFamily` is a SEPARATE trait from `CtrFamily` for one measured reason:
// `impl CtrFamily` is emitted for ordered_map, multimap AND vector families,
// while `{N}LeafBatch`/`{N}LeafWalk` come out of the ordered_map arm of the
// emitter ALONE. Putting the two assoc types on `CtrFamily` was MEASURED and it
// breaks the vector family's OWN emission — `error [impl CtrFamily for
// CtrClass$G1$hs_…]: unknown type 'Hs…LeafBatch'` — and the stdlib build stays
// green while it does, because no stdlib unit instantiates a vector family
// through the factory.
//
// So the capability is a membership (ADR §3: existence = trait membership), and
// THIS is the direction that has to be checked: a family that produces no leaf
// batches must not end up with a leaf walk.
//
// ⚠ WHERE THE REFUSAL ACTUALLY LANDS, MEASURED, AND THE HOLE THAT LEAVES.
// The refusal below is at the METHOD (`'Hs…' has no method 'leaf_batches'`),
// NOT at the projection. The projection `<typeof(Vec1) as CtrLeafFamily>::LeafWalk`
// is NOT refused for an unsatisfied obligation — it resolves to `<error>` and the
// compile continues (`mlir_gen: unresolved AssocType '<error>::CtrLeafFamily::
// LeafWalk' — mono_pass required`), which in a variant that only PASSES a value of
// that type produced the unrelated diagnostic `call to unsafe function 'take'
// requires unsafe context`. So the type-level obligation on an assoc-type
// projection is UNCHECKED today; this test pins the refusal that exists, and the
// missing one is recorded here rather than left as an assumption. What the test
// does hold is the substantive claim — a vector family cannot be leaf-walked —
// which is the ground for splitting the trait in the first place.
//
// THE OTHER DIRECTION OF THAT SPLIT IS ALREADY IN THE CORPUS: `pass/
// container_item_e2e` instantiates a `kind vector` family through the factory
// (`create_ctr::<typeof(Vector::<u64>)>`), so the arrangement that VERDICT 4
// measured as broken — the two assoc types on `CtrFamily` itself, which makes the
// vector family's own `impl CtrFamily` reference `unknown type 'Hs…LeafBatch'` —
// reds a LIVE test, not only a probe.
//
// TWIN: `pass/ctr_leaf_family_spelling` — the same projection, an ordered_map
// family, admitted and answering. Neither half alone separates "refuses the
// right thing" from "refuses everything".
package ctr_leaf_family_vector_refused;

use logos.lcm.canon.container_item;
use logos.lcm.canon.metaclass;
use logos.mem.bt.map;
use logos.mem.bt.memstore;
use logos.mem.sync;

pub container Vec1 {
    kind vector;
    entry { elem: u64 }
    measure count;
}

// A vector family has no leaf-batch producer, so it is not a `CtrLeafFamily`.
pub type VecWalk = <typeof(Vec1) as CtrLeafFamily>::LeafWalk;

fn main() -> i32 {
    let mut store: Arc<MemoryStore> = store_new();
    let snap: Arc<dyn Snapshot> = store_fork_arc(&mut store);
    let mut c = create_ctr::<typeof(Vec1)>(&snap, 1u64);
    let mut s: VecWalk = c.leaf_batches();
    return 0i32;
}
